# Agent Skills for aave-v3-origin

This repository ships reusable **agent skills** under `.agents/skills/` (installed via `npx skills`, tracked in `skills-lock.json`). Each skill is a `SKILL.md` with detailed, step-by-step instructions.

When the current task matches a trigger below, you MUST read the referenced `SKILL.md` (and its `references/`, `scripts/`, `templates/`) and follow it before acting. Prefer the skill's guidance over ad-hoc approaches. Skills may run shell commands and edit files (e.g. `foundry.toml`) — only invoke them for their stated purpose and review changes.

## Skill catalog and when to use each

- **`.agents/skills/solidity-auditor/SKILL.md`** — Load for any **security review / audit** of Solidity code. Triggers: "audit", "review this contract", "check for security", "find vulnerabilities", reviewing risk in `src/contracts/**`. Excludes `interfaces/`, `lib/`, `mocks/`, `test/`, `*.t.sol`.
- **`.agents/skills/x-ray/SKILL.md`** — Load for **pre-audit readiness / protocol summarization**. Triggers: "x-ray", "audit readiness", "readiness report", "pre-audit report", "prep this protocol", "summarize this protocol". Produces an `x-ray/` report (threat model, invariants, integrations, test analysis).
- **`.agents/skills/fizz/SKILL.md`** — Load when building **stateful fuzzing / invariant suites** for Echidna or Medusa (this repo already has `tests/invariants/`, `medusa.json`, and `make echidna`/`make medusa`). Triggers: "fizz", "generate fuzz suite", "build fuzz harness", "stateful fuzzing", "property testing", "invariant suite". Note: it may add a `[profile.fuzz]` block to `foundry.toml` — review before committing.
- **`.agents/skills/upgrade-solidity-contracts/SKILL.md`** — Load for **upgradeability** work: UUPS/Transparent/Beacon proxies, initializers vs constructors, storage-layout safety, ERC-7201 namespaced storage, validating upgrade safety. Highly relevant here — Aave uses proxy `*Instance` contracts and initializers.
- **`.agents/skills/develop-secure-contracts/SKILL.md`** — Load when **integrating OpenZeppelin components** (ERC20/721/1155, `AccessControl`/`Ownable`, `Pausable`/`ReentrancyGuard`, governance, account abstraction) into contracts. Emphasizes library-first patterns.
- **`.agents/skills/setup-solidity-contracts/SKILL.md`** — Load when **setting up / configuring** a Solidity project or adding OpenZeppelin deps and Foundry `remappings`.
- **`.agents/skills/differential-review/SKILL.md`** — Load for **security-focused review of a diff** (PR, commit range, branch changes). Triggers: "review this PR", "review this diff", "differential review", "check this change for regressions". Analyzes blast radius, uses git history for context, and reports potential security regressions. Prefer this over `solidity-auditor` when the scope is a change-set rather than whole files.
- **`.agents/skills/entry-point-analyzer/SKILL.md`** — Load when asked to **map entry points / access control**. Triggers: "entry points", "external functions", "attack surface", "privileged functions", "access control map". Produces a structured report of state-changing functions categorized by access level (public / admin / role-restricted / contract-only) — useful for `Pool`, `PoolConfigurator`, `ACLManager`.
- **`.agents/skills/token-integration-analyzer/SKILL.md`** — Load when **evaluating a token listing or token-handling code**. Triggers: "can we list this token", "token integration", "weird token", "fee-on-transfer", "rebasing", ERC-20 conformity questions. Based on Trail of Bits' token integration checklist (20+ non-standard token patterns, owner privileges, composition).
- **`.agents/skills/fp-check/SKILL.md`** — Load to **verify a suspected finding**. Triggers: "is this finding real", "false positive?", "verify this vulnerability", "validate this bug". Produces a TRUE POSITIVE / FALSE POSITIVE verdict with evidence. Use on findings produced by `solidity-auditor` or external reports; not for discovering new bugs.
- **`.agents/skills/variant-analysis/SKILL.md`** — Load after a bug is confirmed to **hunt for variants of the same pattern** elsewhere in the codebase. Triggers: "variant analysis", "find similar bugs", "are there other instances of this issue".

## Notes

- This is a Foundry/Solidity codebase; there is no long-running app. Build with `forge build`, test with `make test`, lint with `npm run lint` (see `AGENTS.md`).
- Manage skills with `npx skills list`, `npx skills update`, `npx skills add <owner/repo@skill>`.
